{"w":2400,"lines":[{"w":0.069958845774332645,"x":0.7716049391467531,"c":0.5,"t":"1718867188","h":0.008720930389296444,"y":0.046511627815394085},{"x":0.1172839502042468,"w":0.057613169352213542,"y":0.053779069625663367,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"t":"Test 4"},{"t":"Rocha and his team used state-of-the-art ultrasonic recorders to record over a thousand bat","y":0.097383720817062813,"w":0.72016459147135414,"h":0.011627907185728592,"c":1,"x":0.11934157242352683},{"h":0.016476004368003561,"c":1,"w":0.75113082885742188,"y":0.11305825010582315,"t":"'feeding buzzes' (echolocation sequences used by bats to target their prey) at 54 sites, in order","x":0.1172298180953364},{"w":0.76337448120117191,"x":0.11522634592204763,"t":"to identify the favourite feeding spots of the bats. They next used DNA barcoding techniques to","y":0.13074204962355762,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.4732510375976563,"x":0.11522633295865205,"t":"analyse droppings collected from bats at the different sites.","y":0.14811542991153936,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"c":1,"y":0.18168433448288412,"h":0.01453659587810685,"w":0.69547322591145833,"x":0.11728396307153256,"t":"The recordings revealed that bat activity over rice fields was much higher than it was in"},{"w":0.74485595703125007,"h":0.014723203769140047,"y":0.19758539482778703,"c":1,"t":"continuous forest - seven times higher over rice fields which were on flat ground, and sixteen","x":0.11522634236724344},{"h":0.016019188192342937,"x":0.11522632950185985,"c":1,"t":"times higher over fields on the sides of hills - leaving no doubt that the animals are preferentially","y":0.21366279055168713,"w":0.77366256713867199},{"y":0.23110465103020594,"x":0.11728395993229355,"w":0.77160491943359377,"c":1,"t":"foraging in these man-made ecosystems. The researchers suggest that the bats favour these fields","h":0.01453488398216074},{"w":0.72650639851888021,"t":"because lack of water and nutrient run-off make these crops more susceptible to insect pest","h":0.017398163623607577,"c":1,"x":0.11721041996845391,"y":0.24436847595974964},{"c":1,"x":0.11522633042993931,"y":0.26442873986134152,"w":0.767489725748698,"t":"infestations. DNA analysis showed that all six species of bat had fed on economically important","h":0.014723203769140158},{"w":0.72027038574218749,"c":1,"h":0.016134603565517103,"t":"insect pests. While the findings indicated that rice farming benefits most from the bats, the","x":0.11723102407575596,"y":0.27900373001063494},{"w":0.76954732259114578,"x":0.11522633900043464,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"t":"scientists also found indications that the bats were consuming pests of other crops, including the","y":0.29651162774927509},{"x":0.1172839417233314,"w":0.77983540852864586,"h":0.017496644818740692,"t":"black twig borer (which infests coffee plants), the sugarcane cicada, the macadamia nut-borer, and","c":1,"y":0.31389870417289367},{"w":0.31302378336588543,"t":"the sober tabby (a pest of citrus fruits).","h":0.018043359120686775,"c":1,"x":0.11507360356357518,"y":0.32907687052597123},{"x":0.11516593393507293,"c":1,"w":0.77375422159830742,"t":"'The effectiveness of bats as pest controllers has already been proven in the USA and Catalonia,'","h":0.017362244699251295,"y":0.36171097840640187},{"c":1,"x":0.11728394197294345,"y":0.37926972887215238,"h":0.014723203769140158,"t":"said co-author James Kemp, from the University of Lisbon. 'But our study is the first to show this","w":0.77983540852864597},{"t":"happening in Madagascar, where the stakes for both farmers and conservationists are so high?'","h":0.017881894420538447,"c":1,"x":0.1151863384961221,"y":0.39532865024563324,"w":0.75319076538085938},{"t":"Local people may have a further reason to be grateful to their bats. While the animal is often","h":0.016008916255020766,"x":0.11522634330838855,"y":0.43021201411891696,"c":1,"w":0.73868311564127609},{"x":0.11522634049129446,"y":0.44611307446386705,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054296,"t":"associated with spreading disease, Rocha and his team found evidence that Malagasy bats feed","w":0.75720163981119792},{"x":0.11522632513242798,"c":1,"w":0.74691360473632806,"h":0.016019188192342826,"y":0.46366279055112203,"t":"not just on crop pests but also on mosquitoes - carriers of malaria, Rift Valley fever virus and"},{"x":0.11522634996411474,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"elephantiasis - as well as blackflies, which spread river blindness.","y":0.47965116264114283,"w":0.5288065592447917,"c":1},{"y":0.51148409913066128,"w":0.77572016398111976,"t":"Rocha points out that the relationship is complicated. When food is scarce, bats become a crucial","x":0.11522633771169864,"c":1,"h":0.017667844522968212},{"t":"source of protein for local people. Even the children will hunt them. And as well as roosting in","y":0.52757594597484636,"h":0.01907919264794522,"c":1,"w":0.75525741577148431,"x":0.11516983618245301},{"y":0.54505300350351404,"w":0.77366251627604177,"h":0.01599350750656936,"t":"trees, the bats sometimes roost in buildings, but are not welcomed there because they make them","c":1,"x":0.11522635832288444},{"t":"unclean. At the same time, however, they are associated with sacred caves and the ancestors, so","x":0.11728396180116751,"w":0.75925923665364592,"h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.56242638384807553,"c":1},{"x":0.11522634489678316,"y":0.57848837194692404,"t":"they can be viewed as beings between worlds, which makes them very significant in the culture of","c":1,"h":0.016034596379148613,"w":0.78395060221354163},{"w":0.77366256713867188,"c":1,"y":0.59593023242494714,"h":0.01453488398216074,"x":0.11522632950453385,"t":"the people. And one potential problem is that while these bats are benefiting from farming, at the"},{"w":0.77160491943359388,"h":0.014557139752750747,"t":"same time deforestation is reducing the places where they can roost, which could have long-term","c":1,"x":0.11728395993186752,"y":0.61189634874723564},{"x":0.11522634586304169,"t":"effects on their numbers. Rocha says, 'With the right help, we hope that farmers can promote this","y":0.62779740850083265,"w":0.77777776082356764,"h":0.017667844522968212,"c":1},{"w":0.45905568440755207,"h":0.018501547958320042,"c":1,"x":0.11514200084348024,"y":0.64384992817135733,"t":"mutually beneficial relationship by installing bat houses.?"},{"t":"Rocha and his colleagues believe that maximising bat populations can help to boost crop yields","x":0.11934156682194574,"y":0.6787396937947443,"w":0.75720163981119792,"h":0.013250883392226243,"c":1},{"y":0.69464075356420696,"w":0.77366256713867188,"x":0.11522632951340957,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"t":"and promote sustainable livelihoods. The team is now calling for further research to quantify this"},{"c":1,"t":"contribution. 'I'm very optimistic,' says Rocha. 'If we give nature a hand, we can speed up the","y":0.71075581381411723,"h":0.01453488398216074,"w":0.74897120157877606,"x":0.11728394621591709},{"t":"process of regeneration.'","y":0.72661014347313968,"w":0.20017959594726564,"x":0.11700602675017042,"h":0.016148329623596358,"c":1},{"y":0.8677325579493067,"t":"82","x":0.11728395070901286,"w":0.024691357612609863,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"x":0.66991924052010743,"c":1,"y":0.95314993857250241,"w":0.30612408955891934,"h":0.03370105756887698,"t":"IELTSXpress.com"}],"h":3395}